### Now let me reconsider the mocha adapter's `end` event when aborted

In the original:
```js
} else if (evt === 'end') {
  if (waiting === 0) {
    emit('all-test-results');
  }
  ended = true;
}
```
My version:
```js
} else if (evt === 'end') {
  if (waiting === 0) {
    safeEmit('all-test-results');
  }
  ended = true;
}
```
When aborted, safeEmit('all-test-results') signals once. Good.

But what if `waiting > 0` when aborted? Then safeEmit not called, and `ended = true`. Later, deferred callbacks run and safeEmit signals all-test-results once. Good.

